course: dictionary
lesson: 2927
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and draw is one of them. You cannot pick the right meaning from the word alone. You need the words around it, which is the context. «Tegan draws herself, Mum and the cat» tells you that draw means make a picture, because she is putting them on paper.
explain: Look at «Behind one drawn blind they see the shadow of a bird-cage». A blind is a cover for a window, and drawn here means pulled closed. The meaning changes with the sentence, so always check the clues before you choose. Try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Draw can also be a noun: a draw is a game that ends with the same score for both sides, or a prize chosen by chance, like a raffle. When you meet a word with many meanings, ask yourself: which meaning fits here?
fact: Draw can mean to make a picture or shape with a pencil, pen or crayon.
fact: Draw can mean to pull or take out, like drawing a card or drawing water from a well.
fact: A draw is a game that ends with the same score for both sides.
fact: To draw the curtains is to close or open them; «drawn blind» means a blind that has been pulled closed.
fact: Draw is a verb (draw, draws, drew, drawn, drawing), and a draw is also a noun.
exercise: «Tegan draws herself, Mum and the cat, and worries her picture looks too small.» What does draws mean here? | Closes the door on | *Makes a picture of | Pulls out of a bag | Wins a prize for
exercise: What is a draw in a game? | A game that one side wins by a lot | A cup given to the winner | *A game that ends with the same score for both sides | A rule for taking turns
exercise: «Behind one drawn blind they see the shadow of a bird-cage.» What does drawn blind mean? | A blind made of wood | *A blind that has been pulled closed | A blind painted with bright pictures | A blind that is broken and hanging
test: Which meaning of draw is picking tickets by chance, like a raffle? | Making a sketch of a tree | Closing the curtains at night | *A prize draw, where names are picked by chance | Scoring the same as the other side
test: Kai says draw always means make a picture. Which sentence shows a different meaning? | «Ravi draws a straight line with a ruler.» | «Sam draws his dog in the sketchbook.» | *«Mia will draw a card from the pack.» | «Lena draws the menu for the café.»
exam: In «Jo will draw some water from the well», what does draw mean? | *To pull or take out | To tie a game | To close the curtains | To make a picture
